### ============================================================
###  Integration Model API — /api/projects/{projectId}/model/**
###  The durable, project-owned integration model (V16): sources,
###  alignments (mappings), constraints, and compile → DRAFT.
###  Run auth.http first to populate {{access_token}}.
### ============================================================

### Fill these in from your dev data (see projects.http / datasets):
@projectId = replace-with-a-project-id
@leftDatasetId = replace-with-a-bootstrapped-dataset-id
@rightDatasetId = replace-with-another-bootstrapped-dataset-id
@thirdDatasetId = replace-with-a-third-bootstrapped-dataset-id

### getOrCreate: the model is created empty on first GET, then returns the full bundle.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Enrol the three demo datasets as sources (seeds one model_source per class, with wrappers).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "datasetId": "{{leftDatasetId}}" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "datasetId": "{{rightDatasetId}}" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/sources
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "datasetId": "{{thirdDatasetId}}" }

### Suggest alignments for one pair → rows persist as SUGGESTED with scores in `evidence`.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/suggest
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "leftDatasetId": "{{leftDatasetId}}", "rightDatasetId": "{{rightDatasetId}}" }

### Accept one suggestion (copy a mapping id from the GET / suggest response into {{mappingId}}).
@mappingId = replace-with-a-suggested-mapping-id
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/mappings/{{mappingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "ACCEPTED" }

### Add a manual mapping (created ACCEPTED). kind ∈ class | datatype | object | join.
### For a join, label carries the packed "label|relationship|direction" form.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/mappings
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "class",
  "sourceIri": "http://example.org/left/Paper",
  "targetIri": "http://example.org/right/Article",
  "label": "Paper"
}

### Edit a class wrapper (classIri rides in the body so IRIs with slashes survive).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/sources/{{leftDatasetId}}/wrappers
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classIri": "http://example.org/left/Paper", "sql": "SELECT * FROM ${SNAPSHOT}" }

### Add a constraint (unenforced by default), then enforce it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/constraints
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classIri": "http://example.org/right/Researcher", "expression": "h_index >= 0" }

### @constraintId = replace-with-a-constraint-id
# PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/constraints/{{constraintId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "enforced": true }

### Compile the whole model → 202 with a jobId. Poll GET /api/jobs/{id} until SUCCEEDED;
### its `result` carries draftVersionId and unusedAlignments.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model/compile
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Poll the compile job (copy the jobId from the 202 above).
@compileJobId = replace-with-the-jobId-from-compile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{compileJobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Durability proof: after a server restart, the full bundle is still here.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/model
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json
